FaceUnlock
==========

Third-party components and acknowledgements.

1. SFace face-recognition model (bundled as Models/SFace.mlpackage)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Source:  OpenCV Zoo, models/face_recognition_sface
         https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_recognition_sface
File:    face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx
         sha256 0ba9fbfa01b5270c96627c4ef784da859931e02f04419c829e83484087c34e79
License: Apache License 2.0 (full text in Models/LICENSE-SFace.txt)
Credits: SFace by Yaoyao Zhong et al. ("SFace: Sigmoid-Constrained Hypersphere
         Loss for Robust Face Recognition", arXiv:2205.12010); ONNX conversion
         by Chengrui Wang for OpenCV Zoo.

Modification: converted from ONNX to Core ML (mlprogram, float16) with
tools/convert_sface.py. The conversion was checked numerically against the
original ONNX graph (cosine similarity > 0.999 on random inputs). No retraining.

Note: the upstream SFace research repository (github.com/zhongyy/SFace) does
not carry its own licence file; the weights used here are the ones OpenCV Zoo
distributes under Apache-2.0.

2. Glance (https://github.com/jonnyoo/glance), MIT License
----------------------------------------------------------
FaceUnlock is original code, but its overall approach was informed by reading
Glance: unlocking by typing the stored password with CGEvent keyboard events
carrying Unicode strings, clearing the field first with layout-independent
Cmd+Right / Cmd+Delete, reading the authoritative lock state from
CGSessionCopyCurrentDictionary, and aligning faces to the standard 5-point
112x112 template before embedding. Glance's licence:

